# Raw data. application_train.csv is roughly 158 MB, well past anything that belongs in git.
# See README, "Getting the data", for how to fetch it.
data/raw/
data/processed/
data/interim/

# The SQLite monitoring store and its write ahead log. Regenerated by `make demo`.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
data/monitoring.db*

# The fitted artifact and its frozen reference distributions. Together well under 100 KB, so
# size is not the issue: both are `make train` outputs, and committing either would mean the
# repository could hold a model (or a drift baseline) that no longer matches the code that
# produced it.
models/*.joblib
models/*.json

# The reports are committed on purpose. Together they are about 100 KB, and they are the
# evidence behind every number in the README, so leaving them out would mean the claims could
# not be checked without a 158 MB download and an eight minute run. Only the raw console log
# is excluded, since it is noise rather than evidence.
reports/end_to_end_run.log

.env
.venv/
venv/
env/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
